    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Sensitivity A — Minimum sample size (N ≥ 40)\"\n---\n\n\n\n## What this tests\n\nProtocol §3.7 (first analysis). `ln M` is estimated less stably when the two\ngroups being compared are small, because the plug-in sampling variance can\nbecome unstable when between-group variation is small relative to within-group\nvariation. To check that the main conclusions do not rest on poorly replicated\ncontrasts, every included moderator model is refit after restricting the data\nto contrasts with total sample size $n_1 + n_2 \\geq 40$ — **5,364 of 7,511\ncontrasts**. All other model structure (phylogeny, `ref_id`, priors, MCMC\nsettings) is identical to the primary fit.\n\n## How it was fit\n\nFit on the compute server (`totoro`), not at render. Each model uses 4 chains ×\n4,000 iterations (2,000 warmup), `adapt_delta = 0.97`, `max_treedepth = 15`,\n`cmdstanr`. The book reads the cached summary tables only.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ndat_n40 <- dat_es |> dplyr::filter(n_total >= 40)          # 5,364 contrasts\nphylo   <- prepare_phylo_and_data(dat_mod, A_full)          # phylogeny retained\nformula <- build_ls_formula(moderator, has_phylogeny = phylo$has_phylo)\nfit     <- fit_ls_model(\n  phylo$dat_model, formula,\n  build_ls_priors(formula, phylo$dat_model, phylo$V, A = phylo$A_mod),\n  V = phylo$V, A = phylo$A_mod, mcmc_args = default_mcmc_args)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Convergence diagnostics\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-condensed\" style=\"width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n<caption>Convergence diagnostics (4 chains, 2000 post-warmup draws each).</caption>\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Moderator </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Max R̂ </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Min bulk ESS </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Min tail ESS </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Divergences </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Max-treedepth hits </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> Trait type (m05) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 1.0096 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 807 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 434 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 57 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Comparison design (m02) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0039 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 564 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 966 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Disturbance context (m01) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0041 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 684 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1163 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Environmental-change context (m08) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0057 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 532 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 938 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Phenotypic vs genetic study (m07) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0070 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 494 </td>\n   <td style=